    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "837beecf-4239-4b3d-b683-1d611af3da2e",
      "key": "a1053e8f-9a6c-491e-a8a8-0133334e6271",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Itinerary"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Ch3\u003EDay 1\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EWe meet at our designated pick up points and transfer by private coach to Gatwick Airport for our direct scheduled Easyjet flight to Thessaloniki. We continue to the 4* Porto Palace Hotel at Thessaloniki for a four night stay. A welcome dinner is included in our hotel this evening.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 2\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThis morning we enjoy a guided tour of Thessaloniki, Greece\u2019s second city, founded by King Kassandros in 315 BC. Our guided tour takes in sights such as the Byzantine Church of Agios, Greece\u2019s largest church, the Galerius Mausoleum, the Roman Arch of Galerius, and the White Tower, Thessaloniki\u2019s most famous sight (during the guided tour we only see the exteriors of the mentioned attractions \u2013 entrance fees are not included). The rest of the day is at leisure in Thessaloniki, and on an individual basis you may choose to visit the Archaeological Museum, home to a host of treasures. Dinner is included in our hotel this evening.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 3\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EToday we travel to Halkidiki, home to spectacular mountains and delightful water inlets. Here we visit the UNESCO listed Mount Athos, an Orthodox spiritual centre since 1054. The \u2018Holy Mountain\u2019 which is forbidden to women and children, is also a recognised artistic site. There are 20 monasteries which presently are inhabited by some 1,400 monks, and its school of painting influenced the history of Orthodox art. An included boat trip enables us to see the monasteries of Mount Athos close up. The rest of the day is at leisure. This evening dinner is included at a carefully selected restaurant close to our hotel.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 4\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EPella is our destination this morning, the ancient capital of Macedonia, and birthplace of Alexander the Great. We continue to the Archaeological Site of Aigai. The city of Aigai, the ancient first capital of the Kingdom of Macedonia, was discovered in the 19th century near Vergina, in northern Greece. The most important remains are the monumental palace, lavishly decorated with mosaics and painted stuccoes, and the burial ground with more than 300 tumuli, some of which date from the 11th century BC. One of the royal tombs in the Great Tumulus is identified as that of Philip II, who conquered all the Greek cities, paving the way for his son Alexander and the expansion of the Hellenistic world. We visit the Museum of the Royal Tombs of Aigai. Here we see the burial cluster of Philip II including his golden oak leaf crown. Dinner is included in our hotel this evening.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 5\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EWe leave Thessaloniki today and travel to our hotel in Io\u00E1nnina. En route to Io\u00E1nnina we visit Met\u00E9ora. The natural sandstone towers of Met\u00E9ora were first used as a religious retreat, when in AD 985, a hermit named Barnabas occupies a cave here. Others joined him and in 1336 the monk Athan\u00E1sios, from Mount Athos founded the monastery of Meg\u00E1lo Met\u00E9oro on one of the thousand or so pinnacles. 23 monasteries followed, though due largely to their precarious location, many had fallen into ruin by the end of the 18th Century. During our visit we enjoy an included lunch. We continue to the 4* The Lake Hotel at Io\u00E1nnina for a three night stay. Dinner is included in our hotel this evening.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 6\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EOur guided tour of Io\u00E1nnina, the capital of the ancient Epirus region, introduces us to a city which prospered during Ottoman times when its famous craftsmen\u2019s guilds, including the silversmiths\u2019 were formed. This afternoon we take an included boat trip to the Island of Io\u00E1nnina to visit the Ali Pasha and the Revolutionary Period Museum. Ali Pasha was born in Albania in 1741, and in 1788 was installed at Io\u00E1nnina by the Turks as Pasha of Epirus. Though a murderer, he was a great administrator who made the town one of the wealthiest in Greece. His aim was to gain independence from his overlords and by 1820 he had an empire stretching from Albania to the Peloponnese. When news spread of his intention to create a Greco-Albanian state, Sultan Mahmud of Turkey dispatched troops to put him to death. Later this afternoon we transfer by boat back to Io\u00E1nnina. Dinner is included in our hotel this evening.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 7\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EWe explore the Zagora region today, located in the heart of the Pindos Mountains, and home to some of Europe\u2019s most spectacular scenery. During our scenic tour, we visit the village of Monod\u00E9nri, offering stunning views over the spectacular Vikos Gorge. We continue to the village of Vikos which offers equally impressive views of the Gorge. At lunch time we enjoy a tasting of locally produced cheese and sausage. This evening a farewell dinner is included at a carefully selected Greek restaurant close to our hotel.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 8\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EWe return to Thessaloniki Airport for our direct scheduled Easyjet flight to Gatwick, and onwards private coach travel back to our original pick up points.\u003C/p\u003E\n"
          }
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureDescription",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": ""
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureSummary",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003ENB:- Please note we reserve the right to alter the above itinerary if required for operational\nreasons. Given the historic nature of the places visited, a certain degree of walking will be involved, and this holiday may not be suitable for those with mobility problems.\u003C/p\u003E\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
